# Copy to runtime.env or set ORCH_CONFIG_FILE to an absolute configuration path.
# runtime.env is SOURCED, so every value here overrides the environment the
# daemon exports. Set only what this host really owns, and keep ORCH_PROVIDER /
# ORCH_SESSION in step with the daemon — a stale value here silently wins.
# Both are left commented on purpose. The launcher already defaults to exactly
# these values, and on a daemon-driven host the daemon passes the provider and
# session it wants per launch (`ORCH_PROVIDER=… ORCH_SESSION=… launch.sh start`)
# — uncommenting them here would override that and make, for example, a Telegram
# /start_codex silently start the other provider.
# ORCH_PROVIDER=codex
# ORCH_SESSION=orchestrator
# Provider-scoped model pins. Prefer these over the legacy provider-agnostic
# ORCH_MODEL, which applies to whichever provider is selected and therefore
# hands a Codex model to Claude (or the reverse) the moment ORCH_PROVIDER flips.
# Precedence per provider: ORCH_<PROVIDER>_MODEL > ORCH_MODEL > the pin in
# launch.sh (instance/params.yaml: orchestrator.top_model / fallback_model). An
# unpinned launch emits no --model at all and silently takes the account default.
# ORCH_MODEL=
# ORCH_CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# ORCH_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
# The Telegram /model command WRITES the two provider-scoped keys above (and
# only those two) into runtime.env, so a tier switch survives a relaunch. It is
# deliberately unable to write ORCH_PROVIDER or the provider-agnostic
# ORCH_MODEL: this file is sourced, so ORCH_PROVIDER here would override the
# daemon's per-launch `ORCH_PROVIDER=… launch.sh start` and desynchronise it
# from binding.provider, which decideRelay then rejects as provider_mismatch —
# every orchestrator turn stops reaching Telegram. Hand-editing either key here
# carries that risk yourself. `launch.sh model` prints the resolved state.
# codex-cli's own default is `reasoning effort: none`, which is not adequate for
# orchestrator judgement. Set empty to leave the account default alone.
# ORCH_CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT=high
# SessionStart standing-context load. Codex takes the same hook wire format as
# the Claude harness, so both providers share this one script; launch.sh
# declares it inline with --config plus --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust (without
# that flag codex drops the hook and the orchestrator boots blind).
# ORCH_CODEX_SESSION_HOOK=/absolute/path/to/.claude/hooks/session-load.sh
# Durable singleton lease. The state database must already exist; otherwise
# runtime scripts continue in graceful-degrade mode and log a SKIP reason.
# ORCH_STATE_DB=/absolute/path/to/runtime/state.db
# ORCH_LEASE_TTL_MS=120000
# ORCH_LEASE_FILE=/absolute/path/to/orchestrator/runtime/orchestrator.lease
# ORCH_WORK_DIR=/absolute/path/to/repository
# ORCH_HEARTBEAT_FILE=/absolute/path/to/orchestrator-heartbeat
# ORCH_HEARTBEAT_MAX_AGE=1200
# Human-visible mission-pressure nudges. watchdog.sh is the sole atomic writer
# of this outbox; the Telegram daemon can consume completed replacements.
# NUDGE_OUTBOX_FILE=/absolute/path/to/daemon/outbox/nudges.txt
# FLEET_IDLE_NUDGE_MS=900000
# FLEET_NUDGE_REPEAT_MS=3600000
# NUDGE_RATE_FILE=/absolute/path/to/orchestrator/runtime/nudge-rate.tsv
# Nightly full local test sweep over ORCH_INSTALL_ROOT (or INSTALL_ROOT, then
# this repository). Red suites are summarized and nudged but do not make the
# systemd tick fail.
# FULL_SUITE_LOG=/absolute/path/to/orchestrator/runtime/full-suite.log
# FULL_SUITE_NUDGE_REPEAT_MS=21600000
# FULL_SUITE_NUDGE_RATE_FILE=/absolute/path/to/orchestrator/runtime/full-suite-nudge-rate.tsv
# Comma-separated relative directory prefixes. Invalid values fall back to this
# visible default, which keeps frozen migration reference suites out of runtime.
# FULL_SUITE_EXCLUDE=migration-prep/
# FULL_SUITE_ON_CALENDAR=*-*-* 03:30:00
# Disk pressure is measured for ORCH_INSTALL_ROOT (or INSTALL_ROOT, then repo).
# ORCH_INSTALL_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/installation
# DISK_ALERT_PCT=80
# DECISIONS_FILE=/absolute/path/to/pending-decisions.md
# Turn-end delivery override. Leave UNSET: unset means the hook pipes the raw
# provider payload through daemon/relay.ts, which normalizes it and POSTs it to
# /orchestrator/turn-end. Setting this URL sends the RAW, un-normalized payload
# instead, and no daemon route accepts that: /notify requires {"text":…} and
# answers a Codex notify payload with HTTP 400, while /orchestrator/turn-end
# expects the already-normalized record. Point it only at a sink that speaks the
# raw provider format. (It used to read `.../notify` here, which cost the
# watchdog its liveness signal — see orchestrator-turnend-relay.sh.)
# ORCH_RELAY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9999/raw-provider-payload-sink
# Two-way Telegram MCP channel for the claude provider. launch.sh generates a
# secret-free config into ORCH_RUNTIME_DIR and passes it via --mcp-config, so
# the orchestrator can call reply()/status_update() instead of relying only on
# the one-way Stop-hook relay. The daemon serves a legacy-SSE MCP transport
# (GET /sse + POST /message), so the client entry is {"type":"sse","url":...}.
# Set ORCH_CLAUDE_MCP_URL empty to disable the channel entirely.
# TELEGRAM_DAEMON_PORT=4822
# ORCH_CLAUDE_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4822/sse
# The server name is the mcp__<name>__<tool> prefix Claude resolves. It MUST
# match the reply-routing hint the daemon appends to every inbound message
# (mcp__telegram-daemon__reply); a mismatch silently degrades the orchestrator
# back to the one-way Stop-hook relay. Locked by claude-mcp-channel.test.sh.
# ORCH_CLAUDE_MCP_SERVER_NAME=telegram-daemon
# Claude stalls on an interactive trust prompt (never connecting MCP) if the work
# dir was never accepted. launch.sh fails loudly on that; set to 1 to bypass.
# ORCH_SKIP_TRUST_CHECK=0
# ORCH_CLAUDE_MCP_CONFIG=/absolute/path/to/orchestrator/runtime/claude-mcp-config.json
# Morning readiness report. The Telegram daemon watches this path and sends each
# completed file silently; the orchestrator only writes the digest atomically.
# MORNING_OUTBOX_FILE=/absolute/path/to/daemon/outbox/morning.txt
# MORNING_WATERMARK_FILE=/absolute/path/to/orchestrator/runtime/morning.watermark
